From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - clear the final flag when importing a hash state

ahash_import() restores the fields saved by ahash_export() but leaves
is_final as it was in the request. The import may go to a request whose
context holds anything, for example one that has just finished a
final(), so the next update() can run as a final: it pads the message
and writes the digest to req->result. The self-tests poison the request
context before the import and fail every hash with "update() used result
buffer" in the import/export configuration.

A state is only exported between init() and final(), so clear is_final
on import.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2343,6 +2343,7 @@ static int ahash_import(struct ahash_request *req, const void *in)
 	struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx = ahash_request_ctx(req);
 	struct spu_hash_export_s *spu_exp = (struct spu_hash_export_s *)in;
 
+	rctx->is_final = 0;
 	rctx->total_todo = spu_exp->total_todo;
 	rctx->total_sent = spu_exp->total_sent;
 	rctx->is_sw_hmac = spu_exp->is_sw_hmac;
